// Ch9 B09-B11: the road out, the act break at the Iskarra vigil and the act card (docs/kb/story/beats/
// act1_ch09.md §2 B09-B11). ONE scene with a node per beat, because the cut from D03's walking line to
// P02 is HARD, with no fade (§7): a separate scene would hand the camera back to the field between.
// B09 "The road out" (E, 2.5 min, ~70 words). D01 (35 mm, `ch09_dawn` grade, the last warm light of
// Act I): 05:50, the coast road out of Corrow's landward gate, the broken wall behind. Kerrid is
// waiting at the milestone, standing (he never sits), his straw cape still dark with seawater.
// D02 (85 mm): Kerrid single, looking SOUTH, OUT TO SEA, past the broken wall to the water. Asha is
// behind the camera, OFF FRAME, and never in his eyeline in this beat (rule 3; sweep-G S3). "Below" is
// the sea: Imra under the storm and the held dead. It NEVER means Asha. Rhen doesn't understand it, and
// for once doesn't joke. D02B: Pell has stopped beside them; his crest lifts a little; Kerrid meets his
// eye; neither says anything. One held two-shot, no music change (the only frame in Act I that holds the
// party's two outsiders together; not a reveal). Then Pell answers last night's question, unprompted
// (his tell), and Rhen sees the name-shell at his throat is scraped blank (no answer: Ch10).
// D03 (50 mm, a high wide from a rise): the line forms. Toma first, Pell behind him as he was told,
// then Asha, Ysolde, Liss and Rhen, and KERRID LAST, as on a stair, without anyone telling him to. He
// walks behind the whole line, never at Asha's side.
title: ch09_the_road_out
location: ch09/corrow_night
---
@letterbox on
@camera D01
@music dawn_road fade=2.0
@mark rhen road_rhen walk
@mark asha near_asha walk
@mark toma near_toma walk
@mark ysolde near_ysolde walk
@mark liss near_liss walk
@wait 2.5
Rhen [neutral]: Thought Corrow was where you were going. #line:ch09_road_001
Kerrid [neutral]: It was. #line:ch09_road_002
Rhen [neutral]: So? #line:ch09_road_003
@wait 1.5
@camera D02
@anim kerrid look_at sea_south
@wait 2.0
Kerrid [neutral]: Somebody's still below. #line:ch09_road_004 #tn:"'Below' is the sea and those still under it. It never refers to Asha, who is not in his eyeline."
@wait 3.0
@mark pell road_pell_stop walk
@wait 2.0
@camera D02B
@anim pell look_at kerrid
@anim kerrid look_at pell
@wait 4.0
@camera D01
@anim pell look_at rhen
Pell [neutral]: Pell. #line:ch09_road_005
Rhen [surprised]: ...Rhen. #line:ch09_road_006
Pell [neutral]: I know. You-people say names very often. #line:ch09_road_007
@wait 1.0
@anim rhen look_at pell
Rhen [neutral]: Your shell's blank. #line:ch09_road_008
@wait 2.5
<<set $ch09_pell_named = true>>
@camera D03
@mark toma line_1 walk
@mark pell line_2 walk
@mark asha line_3 walk
@mark ysolde line_4 walk
@mark liss line_5 walk
@mark rhen line_6 walk
@mark kerrid line_7 walk
@wait 6.0
<<set $ch09_kerrid_on_road = true>>
<<jump ch09_the_vigil>>
===
// B10 "Act break: the Iskarra vigil" (C, 1 min). The Prologue frame recurs. A hard cut from D03 to
// P02: the Prologue's broken plaza at Iskarra at dusk, the same seven keeping their separate vigils
// apart (Kerrid standing, Pell with his back to the sea, Ysolde with her book shut, Asha on the steps),
// and Rhen sitting beside Asha. The dusk is a little deeper than P01's, and his lantern's flame is a
// little lower on its BURNER (never "wick": that word is Mother Kell's alone). NO FIRE, NO CIRCLE
// (rule 4; ADR 0017 (e)): the lantern is the only flame. P03: a slow push toward Pell, whose back is to
// the sea; nobody explains it. Rhen's VO, older, plain fact, not foreboding (ADR 0022 (k)): the sheet's
// recommended line (Narrative's first choice). Fade on the burner's flame.
title: ch09_the_vigil
---
@camera P02
@music hush_first_verse fade=1.0
@wait 3.0
@camera P03 blend=8.0 ease=in_out_sine
Narrator(rhen) [tender]: Seven of us walked out of Corrow that morning. I didn't count us then. I count us every night now. #line:ch09_vigil_001 #vo
@wait 3.0
@camera P04
@wait 1.5
@fade out 3.0
@music silence fade=2.0
<<set $ch09_act_one_complete = true>>
// M4-A2P-116 C9: the Act II card is held while Ch9 still hands off to the end card ("The end of Act I"); the scene
// jumps to ch09_act_card again when the flow hands on to Ch10.
===
// B11 "Act card" (C, 0.2 min). Black, "Act II: The Truth": the line's #card shows it as UI's ActCard caption on
// black (M2-FP-121; act1_ch09.md §9 UI 2; M3-C09-05). Then the chapter flow hands off to the end card (Act I's
// credits) until Act II opens.
title: ch09_act_card
---
@wait 1.5
Act II\: The Truth #line:ch09_act_card_001 #card #tn:"The act card between Act I and Act II. Title case, as a chapter heading."
@wait 2.0
===
